WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.413
This is Weave. Our example is a lauhala rose.

2
00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:08.050
Lauhala is the dried leaf of the hala tree.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.833
Here's a fresh hala leaf, before it's dried.

4
00:00:11.383 --> 00:00:18.159
Hawaiian weavers used lauhala for mats, baskets, and sails, because it can get wet and keep its shape.

5
00:00:18.909 --> 00:00:23.788
A lauhala rose is a small coiled flower, made from a strip of that leaf.

6
00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:27.871
Here's how it's made. Hold one strip as a base.

7
00:00:27.921 --> 00:00:30.372
Fold another strip over it, and roll.

8
00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:32.700
Keep folding and rolling.

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.267
When the coil is the size you want, finish and secure it.

10
00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:38.695
The rose is the result.

11
00:00:38.745 --> 00:00:41.250
The steps are what you follow to get there.

12
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.650
This page is virtual, so you don't need real leaves.

13
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:51.707
The photos are your reference, and the model is simplified, not complete weaving directions.

14
00:00:52.657 --> 00:00:58.866
The lesson splits the work into ten photo cards: a symbol on top, and a step underneath.

15
00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:01.100
Here's the cylinder card.

16
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:05.624
Roll the vertical part of the leaf toward the left, along the top edge.

17
00:01:06.374 --> 00:01:08.908
Sequence means the order of the steps.

18
00:01:08.958 --> 00:01:12.007
Put the cards in order, and you've made a sequence.

19
00:01:12.757 --> 00:01:16.377
To build yours, tap a card, and it joins your sequence.

20
00:01:16.427 --> 00:01:20.218
Tap it again to undo it. Reset clears the whole order.

21
00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:28.604
The full ten-card order is still being checked with a weaver, so your order is saved, not graded as right or wrong.

22
00:01:29.354 --> 00:01:32.157
Now you try. Which order would you try?

23
00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:34.208
Pause if you need more time.

24
00:01:38.158 --> 00:01:41.246
Next, a dependency. Choose two cards.

25
00:01:41.296 --> 00:01:45.225
Say which must come first, and what changes in the material.

26
00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:49.807
The page gives two clues. The lightning card says, Start.

27
00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:52.623
The moon card says, Pau, the finish tuck.

28
00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:54.638
Here's the idea.

29
00:01:54.688 --> 00:01:59.704
A step changes the leaf, and that change is what makes a later step possible.

30
00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:01.540
Pick your pair.

31
00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.563
What has to happen first, and what does it change?

32
00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:10.932
Now, look closely at the cloud card.

33
00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:13.840
It says, fold the horizontal leaf backward.

34
00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.641
But it doesn't say which way.

35
00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:20.085
Two people can follow the same words, and fold differently.

36
00:02:20.735 --> 00:02:24.082
An unclear step can still be part of an algorithm.

37
00:02:25.232 --> 00:02:29.572
Last, a sequence where every rule is on the page: making tea.

38
00:02:30.222 --> 00:02:36.045
Four steps: drink the tea, pour the water, boil the water, and put the tea bag in the cup.

39
00:02:36.795 --> 00:02:39.953
The rules. The water boils before you pour.

40
00:02:40.003 --> 00:02:42.575
The tea bag goes in the cup before you pour.

41
00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:44.657
And you drink after you pour.

42
00:02:45.407 --> 00:02:48.294
Boil and the bag can happen in either order.

43
00:02:49.044 --> 00:02:51.085
Test an order against the rules.

44
00:02:51.135 --> 00:02:53.655
This one pours before the water boils.

45
00:02:53.705 --> 00:02:55.495
That breaks the first rule.

46
00:02:56.245 --> 00:02:57.416
Now you try.

47
00:02:57.466 --> 00:03:01.891
Build an order that keeps all three rules, then press Check this sequence.

48
00:03:05.841 --> 00:03:08.748
Your photo order is saved, not verified.

49
00:03:08.798 --> 00:03:12.328
The tea order is checked against the rules on the page.
